            "most_common_values": {
                "nan": 378,
                "Oracle Database is a multi-model database management system produced and marketed by Oracle Corporation.": 2,
                "IBM Series/1 refers to a family of minicomputers developed by IBM, designed for industrial and commercial control applications. This skill involves configuring, programming, and maintaining IBM Series/1 systems, which are used to manage real-time data processing and control tasks in specialized environments. It is used to support legacy applications and hardware integrations in environments that require robust and reliable computing capabilities.": 2,
                "PRO/II is a process simulation software used in engineering and chemical industries. It enables users to model, simulate, and optimize various processes such as chemical reactions, heat transfer, and mass transfer. PRO/II helps engineers design and analyze complex systems, improve efficiency, and troubleshoot potential issues before implementation, ultimately aiding in the development of safer and more cost-effective processes.": 2,
                "Google Services refers to a suite of tools and platforms provided by Google, which includes cloud computing, data storage, communication tools, and APIs for application development. This skill is used to manage and integrate various Google products like Gmail, Google Drive, Google Cloud, and Maps into workflows, enabling data management, communication, and business processes. Google Services allows for efficient collaboration, data sharing, and leveraging cloud-based infrastructure for scaling applications and services across industries.": 2
            },
            "examples": [
                "Application Remediation refers to the process of identifying and addressing vulnerabilities or deficiencies within software applications to enhance their security, performance, and compliance. This skill involves assessing existing applications, implementing necessary updates or fixes, and ensuring adherence to industry standards and best practices. Knowledge of Application Remediation is used to mitigate risks associated with software vulnerabilities, improve user experience, and maintain regulatory compliance by systematically evaluating and enhancing application functionality.",
                "Apoptosis is a process of programmed cell death that occurs naturally in the body to eliminate damaged or unwanted cells. It involves a series of complex signaling pathways, which ultimately leads to the fragmentation of the cell into small apoptotic bodies that are easily cleared by phagocytic cells. Dysregulation of apoptosis can lead to a variety of diseases such as cancer, autoimmune disorders, and degenerative disorders. Understanding the mechanisms of apoptosis is essential for the development of new therapies to treat these diseases.",
                "HDR (High Dynamic Range) Photography refers to a technique that captures a greater dynamic range of luminosity than standard photography. This skill involves taking multiple exposures of the same scene at different exposure levels and then combining them to create a single image that retains detail in both the highlights and shadows. Knowledge of HDR Photography is used to enhance images in various settings, such as landscapes and architectural photography, by producing a more balanced and visually appealing representation of the scene."
            ],
            "potential_categorical": false
        },
